**Finding two numbers in array summing to target. Array: [2,7,11,15], target=9. Answer: [2,7]. Brute force: O(n²) checking all pairs. What hash-based optimization achieves O(n)?**

```python
def two_sum(nums, target):
    seen = {}
    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        complement = target - num
        if complement in seen:
            return [seen[complement], i]
        seen[num] = i
    return []
```

**Why does single-pass hash lookup work?**
